%% Sangati AI — Manager Rush Dashboard Flow
%% Mermaid sequence diagram: What the manager sees and does during rush hour

sequenceDiagram
    participant V as Vision Pipeline
    participant S as State Layer
    participant R as Rules Engine
    participant D as Manager Dashboard
    participant M as Manager

    Note over V,M: Rush Hour Begins (19:00)

    V->>S: Zone states updated (every 2s)
    S->>R: State transitions emitted

    R->>D: 3 active alerts pushed
    D->>M: Dashboard shows floor map<br/>Zones color-coded:<br/>🟢 EMPTY 🟡 OCCUPIED 🔴 IDLE/DIRTY

    M->>D: Opens dashboard
    D-->>M: Shows:<br/>• Zone A: 🟡 3/5 tables<br/>• Zone B: 🔴 IDLE 9 min<br/>• Zone C: 🟡 2/5 tables<br/>• Entry: 🔴 QUEUE 3 min

    Note over M,D: Manager sees Zone B idle alert

    alt Manager taps alert
        M->>D: Taps "Zone B idle" alert
        D->>R: ACK sent
        R-->>D: Escalation timer cancelled
        D-->>M: Alert badge → "Acknowledged"
    else Manager taps Zone B → Mute
        M->>D: Long-press Zone B → "Mute 15 min"
        D->>R: Zone mute applied
        R-->>D: Zone B alerts suppressed 15 min
        D-->>M: Zone B shown as muted (grey)
    else Manager switches to QUIET mode
        M->>D: Taps mode toggle → QUIET
        D->>M: "Enter PIN"
        M->>D: Enters 4-digit PIN
        D->>R: Mode = QUIET
        R-->>D: Only CRITICAL alerts active
        D-->>M: Mode badge: "QUIET"
    end

    Note over V,M: Rush continues...

    V->>S: Zone B → DIRTY (guests left)
    S->>R: DIRTY transition event
    R->>D: "Zone B dirty 4 min" (if not muted)
    D->>M: New alert appears on floor map
